82
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:36,840
on you, too.

83
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:45,610
♪ It's you ♪

84
00:08:45,630 --> 00:08:47,940
♪ Even with my eyes closed ♪

85
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:47,080
Let's go.

86
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:49,480
♪ Just you ♪

87
00:08:49,510 --> 00:08:51,870
♪ Feel so right to my heart ♪

88
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:53,280
♪ This moon tonight ♪

89
00:08:53,310 --> 00:08:55,540
♪ Brings faded colors back to life ♪

90
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:58,870
♪ And keeps me company through
the endless night ♪

91
00:08:59,310 --> 00:09:00,980
♪ It's you ♪

92
00:09:01,010 --> 00:09:03,170
♪ Even if I forget everything ♪

93
00:09:03,210 --> 00:09:04,230
♪ Just you ♪

94
00:09:04,510 --> 00:09:06,850
♪ Can fill the emptiness in my heart ♪

95
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,400
♪ By your side ♪

96
00:09:08,420 --> 00:09:09,410
♪ Even the most ordinary seasons ♪

97
00:09:09,430 --> 00:09:11,780
♪ Feel warm again ♪

98
00:09:12,830 --> 00:09:15,230
♪ It's you ♪

99
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:19,720
Why did you come looking for me?

100
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:21,940
You sent me an SOS message.

101
00:09:23,170 --> 00:09:24,700
That wasn't an SOS message.

102
00:09:25,580 --> 00:09:26,870
I was trapped.

103
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,900
I wanted to seek comfort from you.

104
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:31,200
I didn't mean to make you

105
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,600
come all the way out here.

106
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:35,130
Besides, security showed up eventually.

107
00:09:38,170 --> 00:09:38,770
I...

108
00:09:45,050 --> 00:09:46,000
I went to the main building

109
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:46,670
to get them.

110
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:52,480
To thank you,

111
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:54,610
let me treat you to a late-night snack.

112
00:09:58,740 --> 00:09:59,290
No.

113
00:09:59,290 --> 00:10:00,210
It's cold outside.

114
00:10:00,210 --> 00:10:01,890
Then let's find a place with AC.

115
00:10:01,890 --> 00:10:02,790
It's too stuffy.

116
00:10:02,790 --> 00:10:04,600
Then... let's get takeout.

117
00:10:04,820 --> 00:10:05,750
Cleaning up is a hassle.

118
00:10:05,750 --> 00:10:07,160
I can clean it up for you.

119
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:16,610
I'll drive you back.

120
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,340
You're driving me back?

121
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:31,140
What's wrong?

122
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:33,760
Nothing.

123
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:35,030
That's nice.

124
00:11:16,530 --> 00:11:18,250
She didn't even message me.

125
00:11:20,860 --> 00:11:22,390
Is she not coming?

126
00:11:23,050 --> 00:11:24,510
Why are you looking for me?

127
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:30,670
You came after all.

128
00:11:33,350 --> 00:11:35,060
You're running around in a cast?

129
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:36,030
Do you want to wreck

130
00:11:36,030 --> 00:11:37,030
your leg for good?

131
00:11:39,530 --> 00:11:40,390
The doctor said

132
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:41,500
it's almost healed

133
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:43,230
and told me to move around more.

134
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:44,870
If anything goes wrong,

135
00:11:44,870 --> 00:11:45,840
don't blame me.

136
00:11:46,910 --> 00:11:49,410
Then... I can at least
go for a walk, right?

137
00:11:55,850 --> 00:11:56,770
It smells so good.

138
00:11:56,770 --> 00:11:57,580
Look over there.

139
00:11:57,580 --> 00:11:58,790
They're selling snacks.

140
00:11:58,790 --> 00:11:59,720
Do you want some?

141
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:04,000
Well,

142
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,580
you're out for a night run.

143
00:12:05,580 --> 00:12:07,580
That'd defeat the purpose of your run.

144
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:08,480
You asked me out.

145
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:09,980
What do you want to say?

146
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:11,280
Just say it.

147
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:12,700
Just say it?

148
00:12:13,690 --> 00:12:14,750
How should I say it?

149
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:16,340
I just feel like

150
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:17,530
you've been acting a little weird

151
00:12:17,530 --> 00:12:19,030
around me lately.

152
00:12:19,170 --> 00:12:19,890
And I feel like

153
00:12:19,890 --> 00:12:21,420
you're always avoiding me.

154
00:12:23,420 --> 00:12:24,830
It's not like you need me anyway.

155
00:12:24,830 --> 00:12:26,630
What do you mean I don't need you?

156
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:30,890
I...

157
00:12:31,940 --> 00:12:33,790
My leg is injured, isn't it?

158
00:12:35,030 --> 00:12:35,790
You've got

159
00:12:35,790 --> 00:12:37,740
so many girls looking after you.

160
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:39,940
Why would I get in the way?

161
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:41,930
What do you mean, get in the way?

162
00:12:41,930 --> 00:12:42,790
I've never

163
00:12:42,790 --> 00:12:44,340
felt this lonely in my life.

164
00:12:48,770 --> 00:12:49,870
Can we still be

165
00:12:49,870 --> 00:12:51,340
like we used to be?

166
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:52,650
No.

167
00:12:57,510 --> 00:13:00,000
Can we still be friends?

168
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:00,870
We'll see.

169
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:02,340
I'm going for my run.

170
00:13:02,340 --> 00:13:03,670
Take your time walking.

171
00:13:05,110 --> 00:13:05,910
Tang Lin,

172
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,200
wait for me!

173
00:13:12,630 --> 00:13:14,760
I thought your foot hadn't healed yet.

174
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:17,130
You big liar!

175
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:18,870
Help!

176
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:27,080
Well,

177
00:13:27,530 --> 00:13:29,050
text me when you get back.

178
00:13:31,010 --> 00:13:31,550
Bye-bye.

179
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:49,570
♪ I look up at the sky ♪

180
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:52,970
♪ And there you are, always by my side ♪

181
00:13:53,770 --> 00:13:56,180
♪ Since when did it begin? ♪

182
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:59,400
♪ I can't quite recall ♪

183
00:14:00,310 --> 00:14:03,400
♪ You became the clouds in my dreams ♪

184
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:06,060
♪ Silent and weightless ♪

185
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:09,360
♪ I wish I could stay ♪

186
00:14:10,060 --> 00:14:13,360
♪ Walking by your side forever ♪

187
00:14:14,930 --> 00:14:17,860
♪ Through seasons of endless change ♪

188
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:20,040
♪ Through tides that ebb and flow ♪

189
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:24,870
♪ Letting moments overlap ♪

190
00:14:24,890 --> 00:14:27,180
♪ As we feel the world transform ♪

191
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:26,120
You're home?

192
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:31,830
♪ I'm just glad I was brave enough ♪

193
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,860
♪ To meet the moon ♪

194
00:14:34,890 --> 00:14:37,820
♪ Gently, I pluck a piece of it ♪

195
00:14:36,170 --> 00:14:36,860
Not yet.

196
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:40,730
♪ And let loneliness fade away ♪

197
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:44,920
♪ All I want is to be with you ♪

198
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:42,600
Text me when you

199
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:44,000
get home safe.

200
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:48,120
♪ That's the only thing that matters ♪

201
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:51,960
♪ Love gives us all ♪

202
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:55,040
♪ Like the moon lighting up every night ♪

203
00:14:55,060 --> 00:14:55,880
♪ You know ♪

204
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:59,140
♪ I want to fall in love with you ♪

205
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:01,970
♪ No matter how many times I say
I love you ♪

206
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:05,580
♪ Clouds, please drift a little closer ♪

207
00:15:06,470 --> 00:15:11,370
♪ I could say it ten thousand times
and never tire ♪

208
00:15:21,490 --> 00:15:23,240
[I'm home. Rest early. Have a good dream.]

209
00:15:23,190 --> 00:15:26,460
♪ Practice the poem of love
time and again ♪

210
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:29,880
♪ Where should I begin
with these soft and low whispers? ♪

211
00:15:29,910 --> 00:15:33,040
♪ The moonlight is
gently cast upon your name ♪

212
00:15:33,070 --> 00:15:37,260
♪ I look up,
and you're always there, so tenderly ♪

213
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,890
You're crazy.

214
00:15:37,510 --> 00:15:39,970
♪ Through seasons of endless change ♪

215
00:15:39,990 --> 00:15:42,620
♪ Through ceaseless tides
that ebb and flow ♪

216
00:15:44,350 --> 00:15:46,850
♪ Letting moments overlap ♪

217
00:15:46,870 --> 00:15:50,260
♪ As we feel the changes of seasons ♪

218
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:54,410
♪ I'm just glad I was brave enough ♪

219
00:15:54,580 --> 00:15:57,440
♪ To meet the moon ♪

220
00:15:57,470 --> 00:16:00,150
♪ Gently, I pluck a piece of it ♪

221
00:16:00,170 --> 00:16:03,310
♪ And let loneliness fade away ♪

222
00:16:03,450 --> 00:16:04,270
♪ You know ♪

223
00:16:04,290 --> 00:16:07,530
♪ I want to fall in love with you ♪

224
00:16:07,550 --> 00:16:10,360
♪ No matter how many times I say
I love you ♪

225
00:16:10,390 --> 00:16:13,970
♪ Clouds, please drift a little closer ♪

226
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:19,760
♪ I could say it ten thousand times
and never tire ♪

227
00:16:38,890 --> 00:16:40,170
Morning, Lili.

228
00:16:41,030 --> 00:16:42,240
Morning, Tangy.

229
00:16:46,670 --> 00:16:48,630
Why are your dark circles so bad?

230
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:50,720
Yours are pretty bad, too.

231
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:51,770
Didn't you sleep?

232
00:16:52,890 --> 00:16:53,980
Don't mention it.

233
00:16:54,390 --> 00:16:57,130
A mosquitokept me up all night.

234
00:16:57,670 --> 00:16:58,480
A mosquito?

235
00:17:00,170 --> 00:17:01,270
I couldn't kill it

236
00:17:01,300 --> 00:17:02,460
or shoo it away.

237
00:17:02,870 --> 00:17:04,180
It kept me awake all night.

238
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:05,140
So annoying.

239
00:17:05,140 --> 00:17:05,829
No way.

240
00:17:05,829 --> 00:17:08,359
How are there mosquitoes
out in this weather?

241
00:17:10,810 --> 00:17:13,500
So what did this mosquito look like?

242
00:17:13,770 --> 00:17:15,740
Did it have a bad leg,

243
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:17,030
wear a cast, and...

244
00:17:19,190 --> 00:17:20,640
Don't mention him to me.

245
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:22,240
What about you?

246
00:17:22,589 --> 00:17:23,530
Were you also

247
00:17:23,530 --> 00:17:24,740
kept awake

248
00:17:24,740 --> 00:17:25,829
by a big mosquito?

249
00:17:26,630 --> 00:17:28,380
I wasn't having trouble sleeping.

250
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:29,770
I stayed up all night

251
00:17:29,770 --> 00:17:31,090
making a drone.

252
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:32,900
Why are you making a drone?

253
00:17:35,690 --> 00:17:37,670
I should've asked that.

254
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:39,790
Let's drop it.

255
00:17:39,790 --> 00:17:40,980
I have to go restock.

256
00:17:41,590 --> 00:17:42,400
I've got some ready-made ones here.

257
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:43,440
I'll pack one for you.

258
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:44,170
I'm on a diet.

259
00:17:45,480 --> 00:17:46,830
Why are you on a diet?

260
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:14,180
Li.

261
00:18:14,180 --> 00:18:15,640
Did you deliver the gift?

262
00:18:15,940 --> 00:18:17,770
Why are you so worked up about it so early

263
00:18:17,770 --> 00:18:19,240
instead of going to class?

264
00:18:20,250 --> 00:18:20,940
Li.

265
00:18:20,940 --> 00:18:22,050
I've sent you

266
00:18:22,050 --> 00:18:23,650
the thank-you red envelope.

267
00:18:23,790 --> 00:18:25,500
Isn't that what you owe me?

268
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:26,920
Li, please.

269
00:18:27,030 --> 00:18:28,960
Can you deliver it for me tomorrow?

270
00:18:31,330 --> 00:18:32,830
Let me make this clear.

271
00:18:33,030 --> 00:18:34,360
I'm against puppy love.

272
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:36,350
I know, I know.

273
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,780
What's that on your desk?

274
00:18:38,900 --> 00:18:39,720
A drone?

275
00:18:42,250 --> 00:18:43,140
Nothing.

276
00:18:43,530 --> 00:18:44,400
It's a gift.

277
00:18:45,880 --> 00:18:48,220
Is it for Shize?

278
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:49,880
Nonsense.

279
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:52,000
Don't worry, Li.

280
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,070
I'll wait until college

281
00:18:53,070 --> 00:18:54,500
to start dating, just like you.

282
00:18:54,500 --> 00:18:55,010
Then

283
00:18:55,010 --> 00:18:56,900
I'll give her a drone, too.

284
00:18:57,330 --> 00:18:58,940
If you keep running your mouth,

285
00:18:58,940 --> 00:18:59,940
I might just send your gift

286
00:18:59,940 --> 00:19:01,140
back to you.

287
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:02,340
No, no, no.

288
00:19:02,420 --> 00:19:03,740
